              "engine/status/status.go: all five hook checks now take the installed binary path (hookCommand) and match it together with the family token. The two base hooks use the minimalism token, SessionEnd uses sync-trigger, the Bash hook uses review-receipt, and the shaper guard receives the path. Failure notes name both path and token through the shared referencing helper.",
              "engine/status/status_test.go covers the changed behaviour: notes for an empty hooks object and for missing families, a shell-quoted binary, another path with the same binary name, the binary without the minimalism word, matcher handling, and every hook family under another home (labelPrompt, labelAgent, labelSession, labelReceipt, labelShaper).",
              "engine/cmd/status_golden_test.go adds a golden case for the two base hooks without the minimalism word, and the previous base-hooks-only case now carries the real token so it keeps its intent. The golden files change only the hook notes plus the new case, which is consistent with the requested change to status output recorded in odd/tasks/consolidation-phase9.md.",
              "I could not see the engine/settings helpers (HasLabdrianMinimalismHook, LabdrianMinimalismIdentity, and the variadic HasMatchedHookContaining and HasHookContaining) because they are outside this candidate, so I judged their semantics only from the tests and goldens. The path match for the non-minimalism hooks may be a plain substring, which would also accept a longer path that begins with the installed one. That was not visible here and no test asserts it either way, so I did not raise a finding."
